[heap] Treat zero embedder allocation throughput as a low allocation rate

Since https://crrev.com/c/5935313 allocation throughput is tracked with
SmoothedBytesAndDuration, which has no lower bound. An isolate whose
sampled CppHeap allocation throughput is exactly 0 -- it has never
allocated there, or the smoothed value decayed to 0 after a long idle
period -- gets mutator utilization 0 from ComputeMutatorUtilizationImpl()
("maximal allocation"). HasLowAllocationRate() is then never true and the
MemoryReducer cannot start a GC through its low-allocation condition;
only the 100s watchdog can. Node.js hits this for any process that does
not use node:vm.

Zero allocation is the lowest possible allocation rate; report it as
such. Positive throughput keeps the existing comparison against the
embedder GC speed, so isolates that allocate on the CppHeap are
unaffected.

Bug: 570738027

diff --git a/src/heap/heap.cc b/src/heap/heap.cc
--- a/src/heap/heap.cc
+++ b/src/heap/heap.cc
@@ -3540,8 +3540,15 @@ bool Heap::HasLowOldGenerationAllocationRate() {
 }
 
 bool Heap::HasLowEmbedderAllocationRate() {
+  const double embedder_allocation_rate =
+      tracer()->EmbedderAllocationThroughputInBytesPerMillisecond();
+  // A sampled CppHeap allocation throughput of exactly 0 is the lowest
+  // possible allocation rate. ComputeMutatorUtilization() would otherwise
+  // treat a mutator speed of 0 as maximal allocation and the memory reducer
+  // could not start through its low-allocation condition.
+  if (embedder_allocation_rate == 0) return true;
   double mu = ComputeMutatorUtilization(
-      "Embedder", tracer()->EmbedderAllocationThroughputInBytesPerMillisecond(),
+      "Embedder", embedder_allocation_rate,
       tracer()->EmbedderSpeedInBytesPerMillisecond());
   const double kHighMutatorUtilization = 0.993;
   return mu > kHighMutatorUtilization;
